"""Empirical analysis of the degree of independence between subproblems generated by
different decomposition strategies.

For a pair of features (i, j) and a base context S (a binary mask over the remaining
features), the second-order interaction (epistasis) under the wrapper fitness f is

    delta_ij(S) = [f(S + i + j) - f(S + j)] - [f(S + i) - f(S)]

If the contributions of i and j were additive (separable), delta_ij(S) = 0. The
Interaction Concentration Ratio of a decomposition is

    ICR = mean|delta|_intra / (mean|delta|_intra + mean|delta|_inter)

ICR ~ 0.5 means the partition captures no interaction structure; ICR -> 1 means
interactions are concentrated inside subcomponents, i.e. the subproblems are close to
independent of one another.
"""

import logging
import os
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path

import numpy as np
from sklearn.metrics import balanced_accuracy_score
from sklearn.neighbors import KNeighborsClassifier

logging.disable(logging.CRITICAL)

